Nusummit conducted a security assessment of the Excel-based Market1 add-in application using a custom-developed testing approach aligned with OWASP testing guidelines. The assessment focused on identifying vulnerabilities within the add-in, underlying DLL components, and associated configuration files stored in shared network locations. Particular attention was given to how the application handles sensitive data, authentication mechanisms, and integration with backend database and LDAP services.

During the engagement, the team evaluated multiple security areas including input validation within Excel functions, potential injection points, insecure credential storage, and exposure of sensitive configuration data. The assessment also covered risks related to unsigned binaries, improper cryptographic implementations, and insecure communication protocols (e.g., non-LDAPS). Additionally, the review examined the possibility of unauthorized access, credential compromise, and privilege escalation due to misconfigurations and exposed internal resources.
